ed me afterwards and said i'm  coming to tsm are you sure like he still  want to play with me and then  uh  i called andy and told him yeah sword  still wants to play with me um  and i would love to you know continue to  play for the org and andy literally said  no because he's got too much of an ego  reginald hit back with a reddit post in  which he disputed doublelift's version  of events and said that he assumed  doublelift was quote upset because we  weren't interested in working with him  now this was the point where it went  from a public spat about a player  leaving a team to something far more  serious the next day doublelift levelled  some pretty disturbing allegations  against his former boss  people don't like working with them it's  funny that he has his holier than that  attitude about it because  he's like a bully who gets away with  being a bad person  because he's powerful because people are  afraid to stand up to him and that's  what i'm sick of  that when i was talking to my friends  last night on discord that's what i  realized  is that like  i'm sick of  somebody who's basically just a bully  getting away with it because it's in  everyone's best interests and not  getting in his way there have been  rumors about reggie's behavior over the  years but nothing quite as stark as this  especially because it was coming from  perhaps the single most famous lcs  player of all time and one who had seen  many iterations of tsm come and go over  the years there were those who backed up  what doublelift was saying but also  former players who either came to  reddy's defense or at the very least  tried to defuse the situation  surrounding him much to doublelift shock  even cloud9's owner jack etienne played  down reggie's management style as brash  and blunt during the time that he worked  with him so there was a massive uproar  about this and then everything seemed to  die down until last week that's when  wyatt shared an article in which riot  games told them via email that quote we  are aware of the allegations made about  the ceo slash owner of tsm as the league  operator we have engaged the law firm of  omelvany and myers llp to conduct an  independent investigation into claims of  misconduct made against the leader of  this team in accordance with standard  league process wyatt also spoke to a  number of tsm employees one of whom  alleges they were subject to mental  abuse by reggie other individuals told  them of being dominated by a culture of  fear at tsm of being called stupid or  worthless by reggie or being called by  him after work hours to be screamed at  one of wyatt's sources alleged that  reggie would make an employee cry at  least every other week this echoed what  doublelift said when we first covered  this story back in november in fact  doublelift said that reggie's verbal  abuse of players was enough to trigger  mental breakdowns in some of them he  made  so many players cry i don't want to name  them actually because  i feel like it's it's not my story to  tell  so i would just say that he made a lot  of players cry you would be very [ __ ]  surprised  at how many of maybe your your favorite  familiar faces in lcs  legit mental breakdown because of how  badly  they've been getting berated how badly  they were just getting verbally  assaulted now when doublelift raised  these accusations of mental abuse  against reggie we didn't hear a reply  from him but this time we did when he  responded to wired over email he said he  has quote exceedingly high expectations  for myself and i share those same high  expectations with everyone i work with i  have zero tolerance for under  performance i am intense passionate  driven and relentless in the pursuit of  winning it's my nature i set an  extremely high bar and when i feel that  someone is not delivering i directly and  bluntly share that feedback i know i  need to work on my delivery and i am  working to improve the way i communicate  with my team and those around me i  support and i'm fully cooperating with  the independent investigations that are  already underway and will gladly embrace  any recommendations from the  investigators for some people like  cadrell though these admissions were too  little too late had to work on his  delivery yeah i don't know i don't know  i don't like that i know i need to work  on my delivery if 10 years ago he was  flaming dyrus and now he's doing the  same thing still and he's saying that 10  years later he needs to work on his  delivery yeah i don't buy that i don't  buy that [ __ ] personally a tsm  spokesperson also told wire that they've  launched an internal investigation  involving an independent  subcommittee with the assistance of  outside legal counsel and an independent  investigator they added that reggie has  withdrawn himself from anything  regarding the scope nature and  conclusions of the investigation so we  have two investigations at play here the  tsm one has already been mocked on  social media with some people in the  community questioning just how  accountable the org can really hold its  owner now the presumption here is that  any real repercussions will come from  riots investigation and the legal team  they've hired to help them with this but  is that fair to assume riot are saying  their investigation began when  doublelift made his public remarks back  in november but there have been rumors  about this sort of stuff going on at tsm  for years and it wasn't just behind  closed doors in our last video we shot  examples of videos that have been public  for a long time one involved former tsm  top lane odyrus being badgered by reggie  until he finally exploded  i'm playing a game dude  all right i'm sorry for being rooted  then  i'll be home brad you're  [Applause]  another example was former tsm support x  special being brought to tears after a  heated post game exchange with reggie  like you're the best league at your  sport that's why you went to awesome