d than tsmr from their own  investigation but they're not isolated  from it either they have a vested  interest in the success and reputation  of the lcs and that will always bring  any judgment from their investigation  into question it offers the age-old  question who pleases the police them  calling upon the help of an outside  legal team shows that they recognize  this fact but will it be enough to add  legitimacy to their findings in the eyes  of the community in 2019 riot gave echo  fox an ultimatum after their owner rick  fox accused a shareholder in his company  of racism either he steps down from the  org or echo fox would be kicked from the  lcs echo fox left the lcs of their own  accord it's the only real precedent we  have of what riot can and might do if  their investigation finds these  allegations to be true they wouldn't  have any direct power over tsm but they  can draw their own line in the sand and  force their hand now we don't know  exactly when riot will be publishing the  results of their ongoing investigation  but this all comes at a time when they  themselves are paying out 100 million  dollars to current and former female  employees as part of a huge gender  discrimination lawsuit settlement by  their own rule book they are within  their right to carry out this  investigation and pass judgment but will  the community see them as having moral  legitimacy when their own record of  employee treatment is in tatters to put  it lightly as for the findings of tsm's  internal investigation they're expected  to be released later this month when  they are we'll have a lot more to talk  about because this story is far from  over  you
 

